{
  "_comment": "Empirical Gaussian timing model for adjacent keypresses. Values are (mean, std) inter-key intervals in milliseconds, sourced from published keystroke-dynamics studies (Monrose & Rubin 1997; Song, Miller, & Stahie 2001; Killourhy & Maxion 2009 \u2014 averaged across touch typists). Used as priors by the OpenSSH subtab decoder; heuristic digraph table takes precedence when an entry is present. The bundled ``layout`` is QWERTY; users can override it (DVORAK, Colemak, AZERTY, custom splits, etc.) by editing the ``layout`` field \u2014 the decoder geometry is data-driven. [v2 schema: weight envelopes added on baselines and empirical entries per scripts/WEIGHT_SCHEMA.md; metadata.schemaVersion = 2.]",
  "version": 1,
  "metadata": {
    "schemaVersion": 2,
    "lastUpdated": "2026-08-17",
    "notes": "Weight envelopes added on baselines (5 categories) and empirical entries (124 digraphs). Reader compatibility: weight is a sibling key of mean/std, so v1 readers that only access entry.mean / entry.std keep working unchanged. See scripts/WEIGHT_SCHEMA.md for the field definitions and scripts/merge_empirical.py for the auto-migrator."
  },
